<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="60f80190">The cost forecast is a financial calculation to help adapt cost planning to constantly changing
circumstances. The cost to complete determines and values the remaining activities on the basis of the plan, forecast, and
actual values in the project financials. The resulting figure is arrived at by adding the actual and commitment costs
already incurred in the project to the updated cost to complete.</attribute>
